Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: enable airtime queue limits

Every user of AQL inside mac80211 is gated on
NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AQL: the charge in ieee80211_tx_dequeue(), the check
in ieee80211_txq_airtime_check() and the aql_txq_limit debugfs knob. ath11k
sets none of them, and it keeps no queue of its own, so on a saturated
download every queued byte sits in the hardware TX rings where there is
neither AQM nor flow separation, and aql_txq_limit has the same effect at
any setting, which is none.

Set the bit. On its own this changes nothing at the default limit, because
the queue only reaches the 12000 us high limit at peaks; it is what makes
a lower limit reach the hardware at all.

Note that the airtime mac80211 estimates per frame runs below what the
radio reports for the same station (a ratio near 1.85 in the author's
measurements), because ieee80211_rate_expected_tx_airtime() amortises the
overhead over an assumed aggregate while the hardware counts the whole
frame exchange sequence. The limit is therefore expressed in estimated,
not measured, airtime.

This is a backport of patch 2/9 of the series

  [PATCH ath-next v3 0/9] wifi: ath11k: airtime queue limits, fairness and
  a driver TXQ scheduler

posted to linux-wireless by Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
(message-id 20260824142350.1757379-1-julius@bairaktaris.de). The series is
not merged upstream yet and the original diffs were not reachable from the
build host, so the change was reimplemented against backports 6.18.26 from
the series description. It therefore carries no upstream Signed-off-by and
may differ from the patch that eventually lands.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
index c2b9b87..88b3478 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -10432,6 +10432,13 @@ static int __ath11k_mac_register(struct ath11k *ar)
 
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(ar->hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_CQM_RSSI_LIST);
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(ar->hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_STA_TX_PWR);
+
+	/* Without this bit every AQL user inside mac80211 is a no-op: no
+	 * airtime is charged on dequeue, aql_txq_limit has no effect, and the
+	 * whole download backlog sits in the hardware TX rings where there is
+	 * no AQM and no flow separation.
+	 */
+	wiphy_ext_feature_set(ar->hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AQL);
 	if (test_bit(WMI_TLV_SERVICE_BSS_COLOR_OFFLOAD,
 		     ar->ab->wmi_ab.svc_map)) {
 		wiphy_ext_feature_set(ar->hw->wiphy,
